    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building. Where this is not possible the type and treatment of the materials to be used shall be agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to any above ground works being carried out.  \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.\r",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the . Fire Safety (London Plan Policy D12A) included within the Design & Access Statement by Garfield Bailey - Architect Date: September 2025 in compliance under Policy D12 Fire Safety unless otherwise approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.\r",
    "No windows shall be installed in the side elevation of the permitted development at loft floor level.\r\rReason:  To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers in accordance with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
